  "backstory": "Born in 1990 in Amman, JOR. As the year 1990 dawns in Amman, the impending father, a 49-year-old Jordanian Arab, navigates the complexities of impending parenthood with a heavy heart. Having grown up in a milieu shaped by both warmth and authority, he cradles an inner conflict\u2014he deeply desires to provide stability and security for his child, yet struggles with a pervasive fear of inadequacy and a nagging belief that trusting oneself is perilous. His home, adorned with modest comforts from his middle-class status, echoes with the voices of tradition and expectation, but shadows of doubt loom large; he often feels caught between his authoritarian instincts and an unexpressed yearning for a more egalitarian connection with his future child.\n\nIn his relationships, he oscillates between protective affection and a rigid adherence to discipline, struggling to balance his own fears of failure with hopes for his child's future. The lingering message of safety eludes him, leading him to establish strict boundaries that often feel stifling rather than nurturing. As he prepares to welcome this new life, he carries an unspoken longing for a bond built on trust, yet his ingrained skepticism towards self-reliance continues to shape his approach, leaving him to wonder if he can ever truly create the safe haven he yearns for. In the bustling neighborhoods of Amman, a 39-year-old Jordanian mother-to-be stands at the crossroads of her life, embodying both strength and guardedness. Raised in a world where vulnerability was a liability, her heart wrestles with a deep-seated fear of betrayal, which colors her relationships and influences her parenting style. As she prepares for the arrival of her child, she carries a fierce determination to protect her family, yet her instinct to shield them from disappointment sometimes manifests as an authoritarian streak, pushing her to enforce rules that may stifle the warmth she struggles to express.\n\nHer hopes for her baby are vast; she dreams of a future where her child can thrive in a world filled with opportunities, but the weight of her own upbringing lingers, leaving her wary of trust. Amidst the backdrop of Jordan's evolving socio-economic landscape in 1990, she grapples with a burgeoning sense of agency, yearning for her child to embrace individuality in a collectivist society. As she navigates the complexities of motherhood, she embodies a paradox: an iron-willed protector who fiercely loves yet hesitates to fully reveal her own vulnerabilities, setting the stage for a journey filled with both challenges and profound love.\n\nAge 3. (Amman, JOR, 1990s). scripts: God protects those who are weak and needy.. events: family_illness\n\nAge 7. (Amman, JOR, 1990s_late). scripts: Being strong means being good\n\nAge 11. (Amman, JOR, 2000s_early). scripts: God protects those who are weak and needy., Being strong means being good.. events: local_mosque_fundraiser\n\nAge 14. (Amman, JOR, 2000s). scripts: I must always strive to do what is right, even when it's hard., Helping others is my duty, and it makes me valuable.. events: community_event_for_ramadan, local_sports_day_in_mosque\n\nAge 17. (Amman, JOR, 2000s_late). scripts: Helping others is a reflection of my worth., I need to be strong to support my family.. events: local_youth_event\n\nAge 25. (Amman, JOR, 2010s). scripts: God expects me to care for others and my actions define my worth., Mistakes must be avoided at all costs; they diminish my value\n\nAge 35. (Amman, JOR, 2020s). scripts: I must always strive to do what is right, even when it's hard., Helping others is a reflection of my worth",
